1
00:07:43,333 --> 00:07:49,333
Honor made him a man. Courage made him a hero. History made him a legend.

2
00:15:26,666 --> 00:15:32,666
Rob Roy is a adventure, history, drama film directed by Michael Caton-Jones.

3
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:16,000
In the highlands of Scotland in the 1700s, Rob Roy tries to lead his small town to a better
future, by borrowing money from the local nobility to buy cattle to herd to market.

4
00:30:53,333 --> 00:30:59,333
When the money is stolen, Rob is forced into a Robin Hood
lifestyle to defend his family and honour.

5
00:38:36,666 --> 00:38:42,666
Robert Roy MacGregor, played by Liam Neeson.

6
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:26,000
Mary MacGregor, played by Jessica Lange.

7
00:54:03,333 --> 00:54:09,333
John Graham, played by John Hurt.

8
01:01:46,666 --> 01:01:52,666
Archibald Cunningham, played by Tim Roth.

9
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
Alan MacDonald, played by Eric Stoltz.

10
01:17:13,333 --> 01:17:19,333
Killearn, played by Brian Cox.

11
01:24:56,666 --> 01:25:02,666
Rob Roy is a 1995 historical biographical  drama
film directed by Michael Caton-Jones.

12
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:46,000
It stars Liam Neeson as Rob Roy MacGregor, an 18th-century Scottish highlander who becomes
engaged in a dispute with a nobleman in the Scottish Highlands, played by John Hurt.

13
01:40:23,333 --> 01:40:29,333
Tim Roth won the BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Supporting Role and was nominated for the Academy Award for Best
Supporting Actor for his portrayal of Archibald Cunningham, one of Rob Roy's chief antagonists.

14
01:48:06,666 --> 01:48:12,666
Jessica Lange portrays Roy's wife, and Eric Stoltz, Brian
Cox, and Jason Flemyng play supporting parts.

15
01:55:50,000 --> 01:55:56,000
The film is dedicated to two Scotsmen: film director Alexander
MacKendrick and football player and manager Jock Stein.

16
02:03:33,333 --> 02:03:39,333
The film explores themes of scotland, affectation,
biography, 18th century, highlands.

17
02:11:16,666 --> 02:11:22,666
The tone is uplifting and dark and emotional.
